Description: Desktop Icons NG: Manage the desktop window before it is mapped, so that it receives no keyboard focus.
 Desktop Icons NG makes the window of its desktop process a desktop window, kept below the other windows and out of
 the window list, once mutter has mapped it. When mutter maps it, it is still a normal window, which mutter focuses,
 so the desktop had the keyboard focus for a moment whenever Desktop Icons NG started its process: at login, after
 the process ended, and when the process showed no window within 3 seconds. Keys typed into the focused window at
 that moment went to the desktop. The window is now managed when mutter creates it, before it is mapped.
 .
 The change backports commit 135d5440 of Desktop Icons NG by Marco Trevisan (fe64c11b of Ubuntu's Desktop Icons NG),
 released in 51.0.9 of its GTK 4 port, to the GTK 3 version of Ubuntu 26.04.
Author: Mitar
Origin: backport, https://gitlab.com/rastersoft/desktop-icons-ng/-/commit/135d54400253b2dfbf300dc12e283cdd2180338f
